id: pm-github-webhook-inbox
title: Reconcile authenticated GitHub webhooks through a durable deduplicating inbox
description: "Explicitly supplied issue webhook deliveries are signature verified before durable intake, deduplicated, and reconciled against current provider state into bounded proposals."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[3]: changelog-unreleased,github,webhooks
created_at: "2026-10-21T20:34:29.731Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-21T21:14:04.296Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: Duplicate and out-of-order events do not regress lifecycle; signature failures cause zero writes; polling refresh remains a recovery route; typed SDK and CLI with compact TOON/JSON refusals and remedies; real public-tracker copy validation without git; npm and Bun CI gates pass.
comments[8]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-21T20:34:36.573Z",codex-agent,"Overlap audit: existing refresh.ts polls only explicitly linked issues and owns update-only import transactions. Installed CLI MCP tool definitions transport pm commands, with no authenticated GitHub event inbox. pm-observer src/ingest.ts and export-adapters.ts ingest agent exports, not provider webhooks. No duplicate feature found by tracker search. PR #164 owns historical tracker reconciliation; its items remain untouched. Design: authenticate exact payload bytes before all writes; store minimal durable delivery hints; reconcile via current-provider refresh previews only; retain receipts and retry failures. Polling refresh remains the apply and recovery route."
  "2026-10-21T20:41:00.447Z",codex-agent,"Implementation: authenticated intake stores minimal immutable delivery hints; token-owned writer locking serializes concurrent deduplication; atomically published receipts are file/directory-flushed before acknowledgment. Reconciliation coalesces selected issue numbers and uses read-only current-provider refresh previews, persisting compact outcome receipts without item changes. No receiver is installed. Local targeted suite: 7/7 passing, new webhooks.ts measured 100% statements/branches/functions/lines. No-git acceptance removes git from PATH and sets a discovery ceiling. CI now invokes explicit npm and Bun release:check at unchanged thresholds; full gates run remotely because the host is saturated."
  "2026-10-21T20:43:37.315Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: removing only signature verification from acceptGithubWebhook makes the signature-failures test exit 1 with Missing expected rejection; restoring it passes. Removing only the runRefresh number-scope predicate makes the stale-event test exit 1 because unrelated issue #2 is queried. Restored both functions. Real public-data acceptance: verified the source repository is public, copied main tracker into a non-git scratch project, made original files read-only, removed git from PATH, and hash-checked 294 original files. Measured 144 items, 5 linked issues, 10 accepted synthetic signed hints and 10 duplicates; 10 reconciled, 0 pending/retry, 5 proposals matching a fresh polling preview. All 294 original file hashes unchanged; compact JSON receipt 3274 bytes. No provider writes."
  "2026-10-21T20:44:43.174Z",codex-agent,"The broader local refresh-plus-webhook linked run reached its default 120-second limit under host load after 16 passing refresh scenarios; no assertion failure was reported before termination. Narrowed the linked local acceptance to the seven webhook scenarios (including provider-state scoping and polling apply/recovery), with an explicit 300-second ceiling. Full existing-suite evidence is delegated to CI as requested."
  "2026-10-21T20:45:12.776Z",codex-agent,"Local acceptance complete: pm test --run --progress passes the linked webhook command, 7 tests, zero failures/skips/TODOs; typecheck, test typecheck, lint, docstring, zero-duplication and changelog checks pass. New inbox module has exact 100/100/100/100 targeted coverage. Public-data validation and behavioral fault checks are recorded above. Implementation is handed to CI for unchanged-threshold npm/Bun release gates; no merge or release is authorized. Operational limits: local POSIX filesystem inbox, explicit adapter intake, indefinite deduplication retention, proposals must be refreshed before apply."
  "2026-10-21T21:10:01.817Z",codex-agent,"Final concurrency review found that the common inbox lock spans provider reads, so slow GitHub access can block authenticated intake until its bounded lock wait expires. Separate the intake and reconciliation lock lanes: immutable atomically published hints permit concurrent intake while processors remain serialized. Add a real HTTP delayed-read regression and behavioral revert proof, then rerun CI on the new head."
  "2026-10-21T21:10:54.627Z",codex-agent,"Concurrency regression: withhold the real HTTP provider response, then accept another signed delivery before releasing that response. The separate lock lanes pass; reverting only reconciliation to the shared intake lock exits 1 with inbox_unavailable after contention. Restored the fix. CI npm/Bun release gates now run in parallel jobs, preserving Node 22/26, native Bun acceptance and all existing thresholds."
  "2026-10-21T21:14:01.708Z",codex-agent,"Final local result after concurrency hardening: linked pm test passes 9/9, zero failures/skips/TODOs; targeted inbox coverage remains exact 100/100/100/100. Typecheck, test typecheck and lint pass. Separate processor/intake locks keep receipt acceptance available during delayed provider reads. Refresh previews exclude durable inbox storage; reverting only that exclusion makes the opaque-storage regression fail with provider_unavailable. Repeated public-data validation on this code: 144 items, 294/294 original file hashes unchanged, 5 issues, 10 accepted hints, 10 duplicates, 10 reconciled, zero pending/retry, 5 proposals matching polling and a 3274-byte report. The previous CI run was canceled after both npm gates passed because it predates this fix; only the new head will supply final gate evidence."
